// A fixed-size array reached through a reference carries its length in its
// type, so a constant index needs no run-time check at all.
//
// This is the negative half of the pair with collection-bounds-slice, and the
// contrast is what makes either one informative. genlBoundsCheck is emitted for
// both forms; the difference is what the count is. Here it is the constant 3
// from the type '[3; i32]', so the optimizer folds the comparison and no call
// to 'llvm.trap' reaches the object file. In collection-bounds-slice the count
// is a field of the slice value, and the identical index does not fold.
//
// The dereference is spelled out because a bare 'v[0] = ...' through a '&mut'
// array reference is refused; collection-arrayref-write records that. This
// scenario reads rather than writes, so the plain form would do, but the two
// files stay written the same way.
//
// One function, so that the named check's exclusion in cases.toml is about
// this construct and nothing else.

fn first(v &[3; i32]) i32 {
  (*v)[0]
}
